= Direction of the UGT

The *Unión General de Trabajadores* (UGT) is the industrial and agricultural backbone of the socialist movement. Both the party and the union are linked, one can't work effectivily without the other. As in the party, the Union is divided between moving toward peaceful social reform or open class struggle.

- @reformist_ugt: Emphasize arbitration, discipline, and peaceful negotiation.
- @caballerist_ugt: Push for revolutionary mobilization and strike action.
- @fntt_focus: Prioritize the rural proletariat and land struggles (FNTT).
- @root: Maintain the current balance for now.

@reformist_ugt
title: Enforce Moderate Reformism
subtitle: Focus on the Mixed Jurees and discourage strikes that aren't approved by the union.
on-arrival: ugt_reformist += 1; ugt_revolutionary -= 1; middle_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); cnt_relation -= 5; workers_psoe += 2*(1-dissent); caballeristas_dissent += 4; besteiristas_dissent += 4; cnt_militancy += 1 if ugt_reformist >= 3; ma_militancy += 0.05

Under reformist guidance, the UGT focuses on legal arbitration, wage stability and institutional bargaining. 

While middle-class republicans and business owners welcome the restraint, radical workers and the anarchist CNT accuse the UGT leadership of selling out the revolution.

[? if ugt_reformist > ugt_revolutionary and ugt_reformist > fntt_power : The Union favors reform over other tactics. ?]

@caballerist_ugt
title: Adopt Revolutionary Mobilization
subtitle: Align UGT with the Juventudes Socialistas of the PSOE and prepare for class struggle.
on-arrival: ugt_revolutionary += 1; ugt_reformist -= 1; workers_psoe += 5*(1-dissent); rural_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); middle_psoe -= 4; cnt_relation += 5; prietistas_dissent += 5; js_strenght += 20

Largo Caballero's rhetoric resonates deeply with workers frustrated by slow reforms. The UGT shifts toward aggressive strike tactics, worker self-defense preparations and closer cooperation with other unions like the anarchist CNT.

The conservative press warns of an impending "Bolshevik threat".

[? if ugt_revolutionary > ugt_reformist and ugt_revolutionary > fntt_power : The Union favors revolution over other tactics. ?]

@fntt_focus
title: Empower the Landess Peasants (FNTT)
subtitle: Direct union resources from the cities to rural areas in southern Spain.
on-arrival: fntt_power += 1; rural_psoe += 4*(1-dissent); smallholders_psoe -= 3; unemployed_psoe += 3*(1-dissent);

[? if fntt_power > ugt_reformist and ugt_revolutionary < fntt_power : The Union focuses on the rural struggles over other tactics. ?]

The *Federación Nacional de Trabajadores de la Tierra* (FNTT) receives a large backing. Rural workers organize strikes against landlord lockouts and demand strict enforcement of agrarian wage laws.

Southern landowners react with intense hostility.
